  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nIssued 400 AM MDT SUN OCT 18 2026\nThe upper-level low pressure system will slowly move inland \ninto the Great Basin Wednesday and Thursday. At the same time, \nanother upper-level trough will approach the BC, Canada coast. \nEnsembles have the closed low in the Great Basin rejoining the \nflow and moving east of the area Friday and Saturday. Most areas\nsee a chance of precipitation during this period, though the \ntrack of the low continues to favor SW Idaho zones with the \ngreatest coverage and amounts. The heaviest rainfall totals \nremain focused over w-central Idaho, with widespread 0.25-0.50 \ninch amounts and locally up to 0.75 inches for Thur/Fri. \nThunderstorm chances also accompany the precipitation chances, \nwith the greatest coverage and percentage chances happening on \nThursday. Snow levels will drop from 9-10kft MSL Wed/Thur to \n6-8kft MSL on Friday as the wrap around precipitation ends. \nAdditionally, late Thursday into Friday, a significant cold \nfront is expected to move through the area. Winds through the \nwestern Snake Plain are expected to be 20-30 mph Friday \nafternoon as that moves through the area. Temperatures are \nforecast to be near- or just below-normal Friday through Sunday,\nwith another significant upper-level trough looking to impact \nthe area Sunday.",
